CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ default-constructed through empty pack: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
Body-side sibling of cpp20_requires_empty_pack_expansion: the
new-initializer pack expansion over an EMPTY pack during function
template instantiation.  The target is a class with a user-provided
default constructor so the assertion observes the constructor call
itself; a scalar target (`::new(p) int()`) additionally needs
placement-new VALUE-initialization, which is a separate gap
(cpp11_placement_new_value_init).  Runtime-verified g++ 13 / clang++ 18
(placement-new definition supplied in the harness).
